atlas commons
# The interaction layer above the carriers.
#
# This file was nearly four times longer. Measuring a design document against the
# registry suggested that the whole authorable front end was missing -- object
# grammar, apertures, projections, effects, deltas. The atlas guard rejected it,
# and it was right: ObjectGrammar already owns ObjectContract and ActionAperture
# and carries a witness proving five birth modes behave differently;
# OccurrenceSpine already owns Occurrence in C; SemanticDerivation already models
# FactDelta and already forbids reading one as global invalidation;
# ProductContracts already owns ProductContract. Six of nine proposed entries
# were duplicates of built, witnessed architectures whose canonical names simply
# differ from the fact names they own.
#
# What remained after that check is what is registered here: ten architectures
# that nothing in this estate owns.
#
# Three are the layer that MCP, A2A, ACP and their peers do not supply -- those
# carriers move messages competently and say nothing about what a participant
# owes, what may be disclosed to them, or what a generic pattern means in a
# particular domain.
#
# Five more come from the compiler being bidirectional. Occurrence is both an
# output and an input, so the estate needs the semantic rendition of a live
# occurrence, the distinction between an occurrence it watched, derived and
# caused, a publication path where consent is resolved before an adapter is
# reached, a ranking whose unit is a lawful opportunity rather than a content
# object, and the reference UI estate as declared compiler targets. Those are not
# a `.live` subsystem: they are the upward direction of the central law, and
# `.live` is only where it runs fastest.
#
# All eight began `architectural` and all eight are now `measured`: each carries
# a live witness written to falsify its own forbidden inferences rather than to
# confirm that its happy path works. Where a claim outruns the code the entry
# says so in a known_gap instead of rounding the maturity up.

architecture protocol-contract
  canonical_name ProtocolContract
  family commons
  domain Commons / Interaction
  layer commons
  semantic_question How may several participants interact lawfully over one subject, and what does each still owe the others when the exchange ends?
  purpose The semantic layer above the carriers. A transport can complete perfectly while leaving an obligation open, an authority unchecked or an output computed from information its producer was not entitled to -- and no carrier notices, because none of them model obligation. A ProtocolContract states the information each role must hold and produce, the commitments the interaction creates and discharges, and the authority and evidence that bound it. It compiles into owners that already exist rather than introducing a runtime.
  maturity measured
  source_path engine/core/src/protocol_contract.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_protocol_contract.h
  source_path schemas/control/protocol-contract.yaff
  source_path schemas/control/protocol-contract.cue
  source_path schemas/control/protocol-library.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol_evidence.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol_contract.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol_library.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol-contract.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol-library.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol-program.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/obligation-work.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/obligation-decision-frontier.test.mjs proves ordinary native obligation lowering carries a compact reconstructable typed-decision fingerprint, preserves the existing queue tuple and effect owner, and refuses local diagnostics after commitment or queue changes
  invariant diagnostic role frontiers reconstruct from current native commitments and queue state without a second durable store; local model suggestions never discharge commitments or change their legal committer
  interacts decision-plane
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol_program.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/protocol-library.test.mjs holds all twenty-one CUE-registered patterns against all three conformance conditions, so the library cannot ship one that deadlocks or races, and every pattern must create at least one obligation. It proves contract-net ordering, independent escrow obligations, principal-directed agent obligations, bounded dataset release, foreign preflight, evidence-gated upgrades, and no money parameter in mutual-aid (88 tests, 213 assertions)
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/protocol-contract.test.mjs proves ordering is derived rather than declared, independent checks share a wave, all three conformance conditions catch distinct failures, a complete quote-accept exchange can leave both obligations open, and closure requires each to reach a terminal state with compensated violation history intact (23 tests, 39 assertions)
  witness engine/core/tests/protocol_contract_test.c compiles quote-accept natively, derives its four causal waves, rejects enactment without its role grants before opening an obligation, then opens both shared CommitmentGraph obligations only after every AuthorityGraph check succeeds; it also proves native closure reports outstanding commitments and unevidenced claims independently, and that a contradiction reopens the evidence axis even when a support exists
  node_types Role
  node_types InformationParameter
  node_types CommitmentEvent
  node_types ConformanceCondition
  edge_types requires_information
  edge_types produces_information
  edge_types creates_commitment
  edge_types discharges_commitment
  owns ProtocolContract
  publishes ProtocolEnactment
  consumes DomainProfile
  consumes InformationPolicy
  consumes Authority
  consumes ObjectContract
  interacts commitment-graph
  interacts authority-graph
  interacts evidence-graph
  interacts work-graph
  interacts object-grammar
  internal_calculus level 1 communicative acts -- request, assert, propose, accept, reject, challenge, prove, delegate, commit, retract, compensate -- the small semantic moves a protocol is written from
  internal_calculus level 2 interaction protocols: reusable multi-party patterns (contract-net, quote-accept, evidence-challenge, reservation, delegation, escrow, peer-review), imported from the FIPA lineage rather than renamed as new work
  internal_calculus level 3 domain protocols: a DomainProfile gives a pattern domain meaning without altering its structure
  internal_calculus level 4 combinators: SEQ, PAR, RACE, QUORUM, UNTIL, TIMEBOX, BUDGET, DELEGATE, ESCALATE, COMPENSATE, RETRY, PROVE, DISCLOSE, COOL
  internal_calculus level 5 carrier projection: one enactment lowered to whichever carrier the counterparty already speaks
  internal_calculus information causality: ordering is derived from which role needs which parameter rather than prescribed as a message sequence, so the compiler finds the concurrency that a hand-written sequence would have serialized by accident
  invariant a protocol compiles into SemanticProgramIR, WorkGraph, CommitmentGraph, AuthorityGraph obligations and EvidenceGraph obligations; there is no protocol state store, because a second store would become a second truth about one exchange
  invariant a carrier is chosen after the interaction is closed, never before; choosing the carrier first is what turns an institution into a client of its transport
  invariant a role is specified by what information it must hold and produce; specifying it by the messages it sends binds the contract to one carrier's grammar and makes every other projection a translation
  invariant a commitment created by an enactment is owned by CommitmentGraph; the protocol names the event and the graph holds the state
  invariant conformance exceeds schema validation -- a well-formed message that leaves a commitment undischarged, or that carries an output computed from information its producer was not entitled to, is a violation that a shape validator passes
  invariant an enactment addresses one subject through AddressPlane; a protocol that ranges over an unaddressed set has no place to record what it owed
  forbidden_inference a completed enactment -> a discharged commitment (an exchange can finish with an obligation still open, and that residue is the reason to model it)
  forbidden_inference a protocol projection -> a licence, a listing agreement, an appraisal, or an offer
  forbidden_inference a carrier answering -> the interaction being lawful on this subject for this actor
  forbidden_inference an advertised role -> an agreement to perform it for any particular requester
  forbidden_inference a declared combinator -> an execution guarantee (durability is owned by the enactment layer; a TIMEBOX nothing enforces is a comment)
  forbidden_inference a conformant enactment -> a satisfied counterparty (delivery is not satisfaction)
  known_gap the dependency-addressed program is now registered with SemanticDerivationGraph by cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/src/protocol_derivation_bridge.c, independently witnessed for scoped, targeted and atomic registration. The remaining gap is not graph registration: real occurrence-specific ProtocolContract bindings/enactments are still required before an external braid may advance beyond DomainProfile.
  known_gap native ProtocolContract now derives liveness/safety/integrity and causal waves, opens native CommitmentGraph facts only through a per-role AuthorityGraph effect gate, and closes across native EvidenceGraph verdicts. The standalone Python evidence helper is archived; the Python pattern library and work/program lowerings remain compatibility clients until generated declarations bind bf_protocol_contract_*.
  known_gap evidence_required is checked against the real evidence_relations store, with contradiction outranking support and falsification terminal, and an enactment reports obligation closure and evidence closure as two separate conditions. What remains is the proof frontier itself: this native ABI reports whether evidence currently stands and never whether a claim is proven.
  known_gap the level-2 library carries twenty-one patterns and every one of the ten declared families now holds at least one. That is a floor rather than a finish: the design names roughly a hundred candidates, and what exists is the subset whose information causality can be stated exactly today. A pattern is added when its roles, inputs and obligations are known, never as an empty contract.
  known_gap the Agent Client Protocol is not served by this estate. The commerce ACP is -- verified answering at /acp/products -- and the two share an acronym while being different protocols; a projection list must never read one as evidence of the other.
  known_gap seventeen carriers answer on the public surface today with no ProtocolContract above them. That is the gap this entry names: the projections exist and the thing being projected does not.
  known_gap no second protocol state store exists in native code either: evidence_required, WorkGraph, SemanticProgramIR and carrier lowerings must bind the existing owners rather than being reimplemented as a protocol database.

architecture information-policy
  canonical_name InformationPolicy
  family commons
  domain Commons / Disclosure
  layer commons
  semantic_question What may this actor be told about this subject, and what must be withheld without denying that the subject exists?
  purpose Disclosure as a plane of its own. AuthorityGraph answers whether an actor may act; nothing else answers what they may know. Those are different questions, and collapsing them produces both failure modes at once -- refusing a reader who should see a summary, and disclosing a field to someone entitled only to the record's existence. This governs field-level disclosure, aggregate floors, and the difference between withholding a value and denying a subject.
  maturity measured
  source_path engine/core/src/information_policy.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_information_policy.h
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/information-policy.mjs
  source_path schemas/control/information-policy.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  witness engine/core/tests/information_policy_test.c proves the native evaluator remains default-deny for undeclared fields, has exact audience masks rather than an audience hierarchy, rejects a one-person aggregation floor, returns only a policy floor on aggregate refusal, and defaults evidence release to nothing
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/information-policy.test.mjs exercises native Bun projection over a Tarrant parcel, exact audiences including explicit deny-to-all, non-leaking aggregate floors, and exact evidence release; the C witness also exercises ordered bulk field decisions and denies partial output on invalid input
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh compiles the declared profiles into one candidate per subject kind and audience carrying only the fields that audience is declared to be able to see, and proves the forwarding cut is default-deny in the same direction as the evaluator: the parcel owner mailing address, declared to self and institution only, is absent from the public and market candidates rather than marked there, and asking the plane for it as the public selects nothing while asking as an institution selects the declaration
  node_types DisclosureRule
  node_types AudienceScope
  node_types AggregationFloor
  node_types EvidenceRelease
  owns InformationPolicy
  publishes DisclosureDecision
  consumes Authority
  interacts authority-graph
  interacts institutional-product-contracts
  internal_calculus an aggregation floor releases a count or a median only above a declared population, so a statistic cannot be differenced back to the individual record it summarizes
  internal_calculus withholding is stated rather than performed by omission: a withheld field says it was withheld, because quietly dropping it teaches the caller the subject lacks it
  internal_calculus disclosure audience is read from the territory the request arrived on, so one subject discloses differently to self, household, group, community, public, market and institution without being copied per audience
  internal_calculus the audience list is an enumeration and never a permission ladder: market is not a superset of household, and a rule written for one audience never widens to another by sitting higher in the order
  internal_calculus an undeclared field is withheld rather than allowed, so a field added to a contract without a rule cannot become public by having been forgotten
  internal_calculus a below-floor refusal names the floor and never the population that failed it; echoing the real count back would leak exactly what the floor protects
  invariant read authority and effect authority are independent; seeing a subject never implies changing it, and holding effect authority never implies entitlement to read everything about it
  invariant disclosure is decided per field and per audience, never per record; a record-level gate forces the system to choose between over-disclosing and refusing outright, and it will do both
  invariant an evidence release defaults to nothing; a delegated estate sees exactly what its envelope names of the parent's proof
  invariant a public source having published a fact does not settle whether this estate may republish it; the observation is receipted and the redisclosure is a separate decision with its own audience
  forbidden_inference a subject being addressable -> its contents being disclosable
  forbidden_inference a withheld field -> the field being empty, or the subject not existing
  forbidden_inference an aggregate being released -> its constituent records being releasable
  forbidden_inference a disclosure to one audience -> the same disclosure being lawful to another
  forbidden_inference an actor holding authority to act -> that actor being entitled to read the evidence the action rests on
  witness engine/core/tests/operator_reference.test.mjs evaluates exact artifact-excerpt fields for the public audience through the native InformationPolicy ABI and withholds undeclared fields
  known_gap the policy is enforced across the OGC/RESO/MISMO trio through DomainProfile and Fabric reference excerpts through a publisher-supplied declaration; other carrier projections still answer from their own assumptions until each binds a policy
  known_gap audience is supplied by the caller rather than derived from the arriving territory; wiring it to the AddressPlane territory is what makes the audience unforgeable, and until then a caller naming its own audience is trusted.
  known_gap information-policy.cue supplies the exact audience vocabulary to the Bun projection and bf_information_policy_* owns the native C decision ABI. The former Python evaluator and its test are archived after all active callers moved; the remaining gap is binding audience to the arriving AddressPlane territory rather than trusting a caller-supplied label.

architecture domain-profile
  canonical_name DomainProfile
  family commons
  domain Commons / Domain grammar
  layer commons
  semantic_question What do these generic institutional moves mean in this particular domain?
  purpose The specialization between a reusable interaction pattern and a working institution. Quote-accept is structurally identical for a venue booking and a mortgage; the vocabulary, the evidence that closes it and the conditions of settlement are not. A DomainProfile carries that difference so the pattern is written once and the domains stay honest about what they each require. It also holds the shared meaning behind several industry grammars, so a fact cannot be answered differently by two carriers of one estate.
  maturity measured
  source_path schemas/control/domain-profile.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_domain_profiles.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/generated/native_domain_profiles.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/domain_profile_projection.c
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/domain_profile.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/domain-profile.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/domain-observation.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/domain-observation.generated.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/domain_observation_bridge.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/domain-profile.test.mjs holds OGC, RESO and MISMO against one CUE-declared parcel meaning on the row the live surface serves (account 00000051, 117 E BELKNAP ST, $450,000): the three grammars agree field by field, a deliberately remapped carrier is caught disagreeing on a parcel where land and total values differ, a carrier projecting an undeclared field is refused at build time, MISMO omits owner rather than carrying an empty column, and a field withheld by policy is withheld in all three grammars while the entitled audience still receives it (13 tests)
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/live-carrier-conformance.test.mjs fetches the three deployed routes on aurekai.life and holds the CUE declaration against them: every field the profile maps is actually served, every field the deployment serves is mapped, the live carriers agree on every shared fact for one parcel, and MISMO carries no owner in the real response. It is opt-in for live deployment checks rather than passing on a simulation
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/domain_profile_projection_test.c compiles the CUE parcel profile through the Zig generator, proves the generated native projection supplies the live RESO aliases and OGC/MISMO carrier metadata, refuses an unknown carrier and invalid audience, and never projects the undisclosed mailing address
  witness cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/domain_observation_bridge.test.mjs binds a retained HTML observation only after ForeignTwin and Ingest hashes agree, preserves the retired Python binder's semantic digest, appends once, and refuses drift or the wrong occurrence; cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/vectors/policy_compilation.json holds its runtime descriptor byte-for-byte against CUE
  node_types Profile
  node_types VocabularyBinding
  node_types EvidenceRequirement
  owns DomainProfile
  publishes DomainProfile
  consumes ObjectContract
  interacts protocol-contract
  internal_calculus a profile binds domain vocabulary to the roles and parameters a pattern already declares; it never adds a role, because adding one produces a different interaction rather than the same one in a domain
  internal_calculus an external standard is a projection of a profile, not the profile itself: RESO, MISMO, OGC and EPCIS are grammars this estate answers in, and the profile is what it means before the grammar is chosen
  internal_calculus a carrier mapping renames declared semantic fields and may not add one; a projection naming a field the profile does not declare is refused where it is written, because that field came from somewhere other than the shared meaning
  internal_calculus disclosure is applied to the semantic record before projection, so a field withheld from an audience is withheld in every grammar rather than in whichever carrier remembered to check
  internal_calculus semantic agreement is computable: rendering one record through several carriers and collecting the values per semantic field detects two grammars answering one fact differently, which is the drift hand-written carriers make invisible
  invariant a profile specializes an existing pattern and never defines a new one; a profile introducing its own interaction is an interaction protocol wearing a profile's name
  invariant a profile may tighten evidence and authority requirements and may never loosen them below what the pattern demands
  invariant one profile serves many carrier projections; four industry grammars over one profile is the claim, and four profiles producing four grammars would be its refutation
  forbidden_inference a domain profile existing -> that domain's external standards being satisfied (conformance to RESO, MISMO or EPCIS is a separate projection carrying its own witness)
  forbidden_inference a profile naming a regulated activity -> authority to perform it
  forbidden_inference a shared profile -> equivalent obligations across its domains (the structure is shared; what closes it is not)
  known_gap OGC, RESO and MISMO request their select lists from the generated native parcel profile, evaluated against native InformationPolicy; the Bun cross-carrier/withheld-marker vectors pass. Differential checks against the deployed carriers remain opt-in.
  known_gap parcel, live-moment and social-clip are profiled. EPCIS, CAP, WoT and the commerce carriers answer today with no shared profile behind them, so nothing detects drift between them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bridges. Each names what it carries, what it deliberately drops, and the
# promotion it must not make. All three sources are architectural, so these
# describe contracts rather than observed behaviour -- which is why none claims a
# witness. The destinations are built architectures, and the bridges are written
# from the built side's existing invariants rather than around them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

interaction protocol-creates-commitments
  source protocol-contract
  destination commitment-graph
  relation creates_commitment
  preserves who committed what resource to whom, under which conditions, until when
  preserves the enactment identity, so an obligation can be traced back to the exchange that made it
  drops the message sequence that produced the commitment; the graph holds the obligation, not the conversation
  forbidden_inference a completed enactment -> a discharged commitment
  forbidden_inference a recorded commitment -> the resource delivered
  invalidates_on a commitment is discharged, delegated, violated or compensated

interaction protocol-requires-authority
  source protocol-contract
  destination authority-graph
  relation requires_authority
  preserves the purpose, scope and validity window each role's participation demands
  drops the participant's identity provider; authority holds from a matching non-revoked edge inside its window, never from a session
  forbidden_inference a role being advertised -> any requester holding the authority to fill it
  forbidden_inference a valid session -> authority over the subject the protocol addresses
  forbidden_inference a conformant contract -> a permitted enactment (structure and permission fail for different reasons and are checked separately, so a caller told only refused can tell which)
  forbidden_inference authority over one subject -> authority over another
  authority every role's participation is gated by its own declared purpose, rechecked at effect time
  invalidates_on an authority edge is revoked, or leaves its time window
  binding components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol-authority.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/protocol-authority.test.mjs drives the native AuthorityGraph owner and compares its answers against an independent SQL rule on eleven cases, including revocation, window edges, purpose bounds and unknown actors. It proves a conformant quote-accept still refuses ungranted actors before any obligation opens, and that delegation narrows while cascade revocation closes every descendant (22 tests, 61 assertions)

interaction protocol-obliges-evidence
  source protocol-contract
  destination evidence-graph
  relation requires_evidence
  preserves which assertions must be witnessed before an enactment may be treated as closed
  preserves the cannot-infer set the interaction carries, so a closed exchange still states what it did not establish
  drops the protocol's own opinion of sufficiency; the proof frontier decides what an assertion is worth
  forbidden_inference a closed enactment -> a proven claim
  forbidden_inference a produced artifact -> evidence (it must cross the proof frontier first)
  invalidates_on a witness is retired, or the proof frontier moves

interaction protocol-lowers-to-work
  source protocol-contract
  destination work-graph
  relation compiles_to
  preserves obligations that remain open as durable, leasable work
  preserves deadlines and timeboxes as lease conditions rather than as commentary
  drops the role structure; the work graph holds what must still be done, not who was speaking
  forbidden_inference queued work -> an enactment in progress (work outlives the exchange that created it, which is the point of durability)
  forbidden_inference queued work -> the obligation being met (enqueuing is not doing, and neither is claiming)
  forbidden_inference a failed or dead-lettered work item -> a violated commitment (the queue's verdict is about the work; somebody with standing decides that a promise broke)
  forbidden_inference a discharged obligation -> its work item having run (work is one mechanism for meeting a promise, not the definition of one)
  invalidates_on a lease expires, or its originating commitment is discharged
  binding components/BonfyreControlPlane/obligation-work.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/obligation-work.test.mjs drives the real BonfyreQueue binary and native CommitmentGraph owner: lowering enqueues a claimable item without settling the promise, completion discharges, transient and permanent failure do not violate, repeated lowering is idempotent, and partially completed escrow retains exactly the undelivered obligation (16 tests, 40 assertions)

interaction protocol-admits-through-aperture
  source protocol-contract
  destination object-grammar
  relation admits_through
  preserves the subject kind and the operation a participant's local move resolves to
  preserves the birth mode, so a move that proposes is not recorded as one that declared
  drops the multi-party structure; an aperture admits one actor's operation and knows nothing of the exchange around it
  forbidden_inference an enactment step -> an admitted operation (the aperture still applies its own grammar and authority)
  forbidden_inference an offered aperture -> a completed effect
  invalidates_on the object grammar's applicability bound or birth policy changes

interaction policy-gates-projection
  source information-policy
  destination institutional-product-contracts
  relation gates_disclosure
  preserves the per-field, per-audience disclosure decision for the bound product surface
  preserves the distinction between a withheld field and an absent one
  drops effect authority, which this bridge carries in neither direction
  forbidden_inference a bound capability -> its fields being disclosable to this actor
  forbidden_inference a field surviving into one territory's projection -> it being lawful in another
  invalidates_on a disclosure rule, audience scope or aggregation floor changes

interaction profile-specializes-protocol
  source domain-profile
  destination protocol-contract
  relation specializes
  preserves the interaction's role structure and information causality unchanged
  preserves the domain's vocabulary, evidence requirements and settlement conditions
  drops nothing from the base pattern; a profile tightens requirements and never loosens them
  forbidden_inference a domain profile -> conformance to that domain's external standards
  forbidden_inference a shared pattern -> equivalent obligations in every domain that profiles it
  invalidates_on the profile's evidence requirement or vocabulary binding changes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aurekai Live. One occurrence, five simultaneous products: a human media
# experience, a machine-readable semantic simulcast, a federated fanout, an
# ephemeral social world, and durable institutional effects.
#
# Only one architecture is registered here. AttentionCoolingGraph already owns
# cooling, StandingAddress already belongs to the Matrix, BonfyreTranscribe and
# BonfyreClips are already command organs, and VerticalDiscovery/LiveCreatorRoom/
# EphemeralBoard are SurfacePatterns rather than calculi. What nothing owned is
# the semantic rendition itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

architecture live-semantic-track
  canonical_name LiveSemanticTrack
  family commons
  domain Commons / Live semantics
  layer commons
  semantic_question What did this live occurrence actually mean, moment by moment, and which of it deserves to outlive the stream?
  purpose The machine rendition of a live occurrence, synchronized to the media clock. Without it a stream is an opaque blob rankable only by viewer count; with it, ranking, sponsorship, clipping and institution-formation all read one structure. It is the organ that makes the social, federation and protocol work compound rather than merely coexist.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/live-semantic-track.mjs
  source_path schemas/control/live-semantic-track.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/native-ingest.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/native-ingest.test.mjs drives the real BonfyreSegment and BonfyreClips binaries and checks their boundaries, taxonomy, rank, scores, and cooling without a fixture substitute
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/live-semantic-track.test.mjs checks CUE retention tiers, media-clock partitions, explicit claim promotion, independent corroboration, and cooling
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/live-semantic-track.test.mjs holds the Deep Ellum boundaries against the CUE retention law, native DomainProfile carriers, InformationPolicy disclosure, and the C-backed durable CommitmentGraph
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/aurekai-live-loop.test.mjs runs one stream through CUE-authored semantics, independent claim corroboration, native C AuthorityGraph, C CommitmentGraph, the real BonfyreQueue work lease and acknowledgement, sponsorship, and cooling; seven end-to-end tests and forty expectations prove refusal opens nothing, speech is not performance, a compensated breach remains historic, and distinct observers close distinct obligations
  node_types SemanticEvent
  node_types ClaimObservation
  node_types Corroboration
  state_types ephemeral
  state_types durable
  owns LiveSemanticTrack
  owns ClaimObservation
  publishes LiveSemanticTrack
  publishes ClaimObservation
  consumes Occurrence
  interacts commitment-graph
  interacts attention-cooling
  internal_calculus the media clock is integer milliseconds from stream start and wall-clock time is deliberately absent, so a replay, a restart and the live edge all address one moment identically; a track keyed to wall-clock cannot survive being replayed
  internal_calculus retention is an eight-tier lattice (flash, chat, moment, social, saved, institutional, evidentiary, economic) ordered by how long the estate is willing to be answerable for a record, not by importance; a boolean could not distinguish a reaction from a saved post or a saved post from a settled payment, and those differences decide what may be deleted
  internal_calculus a kind's tier is declared where the kind is added rather than inferred later from whether anything referenced the event, because a tier that depends on being referenced is wrong exactly when nothing has referenced it yet
  internal_calculus promotion up the lattice requires an explicit action or evidence and moves upward only; popularity, reference count and mere survival are refused as reasons, and demotion is refused because lowering retention deletes something the estate already took responsibility for
  internal_calculus hierarchical compression runs utterances to semantic events to durable moments to institutional effects; the durable set is a strict minority of the track by construction
  internal_calculus corroboration counts distinct independent sources; a repeated source and the asserter's own repetition are both excluded, because a noisy feed talking more is not a consensus
  invariant an utterance is not a claim: promotion names an asserter and is an explicit act, because deciding that somebody committed to something is the judgement a machine must not make silently
  invariant windows are half-open so adjacent windows partition the track rather than double-counting the boundary between them
  invariant a surface compiled at a moment reads only what the track knew by that moment; a ranking that could see later in the stream would rank on facts the viewer does not have
  invariant cooling partitions and does not delete the world: an expired event still happened, and expiry is a statement about storage rather than about the occurrence
  invariant sponsor matching is exact on the sponsor name rather than substring; a generous comparison would let a shorter name close a longer sponsor's obligation
  forbidden_inference an utterance -> a claim
  forbidden_inference a claim -> a fact (it is what was said, and saying it clearly or from a verified account does not change that)
  forbidden_inference corroboration -> proof (it raises how well-attested a claim is; EvidenceGraph and the proof frontier decide what it is worth)
  forbidden_inference a spoken sponsor mention -> a discharged sponsor obligation (only the contract knows how many were owed, and only evidence closes it)
  forbidden_inference a clip candidate -> a published clip
  forbidden_inference an expired ephemeral event -> the moment not having happened
  forbidden_inference a popular or much-referenced record -> a record worth keeping (storage is not memory, and promoting on attention is how a timeline becomes sludge)
