architecture occurrence-origin
  canonical_name OccurrenceOrigin
  family commons
  domain Commons / Occurrence provenance
  layer commons
  semantic_question Did this happen to us, did we derive it, or did we do it?
  purpose OccurrenceSpine was read as the effects this estate created. The upward direction of the compiler makes that untenable: one spine now carries what happened externally, what was derived from watching it, and what the estate caused. They are answerable for different things, and an estate that files all three without origin will eventually settle money against a derivation.
  maturity measured
  source_path engine/core/src/occurrence_origin.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_occurrence_origin.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreOrigin/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh
  source_path schemas/control/occurrence-origin.yaff
  source_path schemas/control/occurrence-origin.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/occurrence-origin.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/occurrence-origin.test.mjs files one night on the native-owned relation and refuses observation/derivation authority laundering, missing provenance/inputs, and re-filing; provenance returns only observed roots
  witness engine/core/tests/occurrence_origin_test.c proves native storage refuses source-less observations, input-less derivations, authority-less effects and re-filing; it also verifies that derivation roots are observed occurrences only, never effects
  witness cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh proves the native caller refuses an input-less derivation, stores an observed occurrence and reports its derived successor as not caused by this estate
  node_types Occurrence
  state_types observed
  state_types derived
  state_types effect
  owns OccurrenceOrigin
  publishes OccurrenceOrigin
  consumes Occurrence
  interacts occurrence-spine
  interacts live-semantic-track
  internal_calculus each origin demands exactly what it is answerable for: an observation names its source, a derivation names its inputs, an effect names its authority, and only the effect may carry one
  internal_calculus provenance walks a derivation chain to the observations beneath it; a derivation with no observed root descends from something the estate did rather than something it watched, and reports that rather than an empty observation
  invariant raw material is not an occurrence; audio bytes are not, an utterance is, and the boundary is whether anything temporal and meaningful can be addressed
  invariant an occurrence is filed once; refiling the same id under a different origin would relabel watching as acting, which is the laundering this architecture exists to stop
  forbidden_inference an observed occurrence -> something the estate did
  forbidden_inference a derived occurrence -> an effect (a SponsorOccurrence candidate derived from a transcript is not the obligation being met)
  forbidden_inference a derived occurrence -> its inputs being true
  forbidden_inference an effect occurrence -> the intended outcome
  invariant native C and Bun callers share one occurrence_origin relation and the same origin refusal laws; a Bun facade does not create a second occurrence store
  known_gap the spine keeps causal ordering separate from origin so no caller can infer an effect from being on the spine; a future unified occurrence write must atomically admit both owners without collapsing their semantic facts.
  known_gap the foreign ingest path now uses the Bun occurrence facade, but its relation insert and the independent OccurrenceSpine insert are not yet one atomic admission; neither partial write may be read as a completed unified occurrence
architecture publication-program
  canonical_name PublicationProgram
  family commons
  domain Commons / Publication
  layer commons
  semantic_question May this be published there, on whose authority, showing what, and has anybody checked it arrived?
  purpose Cross-platform publication as a compiled program rather than a set of adapters each holding a token and its own idea of what it may post. An OAuth token is a capability to reach an account; what may be sent through it, on whose behalf, about which subject, for what purpose, to which audience and until when are six other questions, and an adapter answers none of them.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/publication-program.mjs
  source_path schemas/control/publication-program.cue
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/publication-program.test.mjs uses adapters that record whether they were called and the compiled AuthorityGraph, proving consent is checked before any adapter, grants are platform/purpose/window-scoped and revocable, disclosure precedes projection, and an adapter reporting 200 still leaves the round trip pending until a receipt-backed observation
  node_types PublicationProgram
  node_types Target
  owns PublicationProgram
  publishes PublicationProgram
  consumes DomainProfile
  consumes InformationPolicy
  consumes Authority
  interacts authority-graph
  interacts domain-profile
  internal_calculus resolution order is delegation, then disclosure, then projection, then adapter; each stage can refuse and a refusal names which stage closed, because an adapter that failed and a principal who never consented are different problems and a caller told only that publishing failed will debug the wrong one
  internal_calculus consent is checked per platform and per operation, because agreeing to publish to one network is not agreeing to publish to another and that is a decision a person makes per audience
  invariant a target's audience is a disclosure audience, not a routing label; a public timeline and a members-only feed are different audiences even when one adapter reaches both
  invariant a partial simulcast is a different act from the one consented to, so a missing adapter refuses the whole program rather than publishing to the targets that happen to be wired
  forbidden_inference a token existing -> permission to publish anything
  forbidden_inference a grant to publish on one platform -> a grant to publish on another
  forbidden_inference an adapter reporting success -> the platform having accepted it (that is the adapter's account of itself; a round trip is a separate observation by a separate owner)
  forbidden_inference a program declaring round-trip observation -> the round trip having happened
  known_gap the native Bun program gates against compiled AuthorityGraph and DomainProfile but still delegates actual network calls and independent ForeignTwin observation to injected callers; neither an adapter report nor a declared round trip is treated as observed fact.
  known_gap no adapter is implemented. The program refuses, discloses and projects; reaching an actual network is deliberately left to callers, and the round-trip observation is declared rather than performed by ForeignTwin.

