  witness engine/core/tests/standing_address_test.c verifies native territory/action validation, availability-before-relevance ordering even after fifty attention signals, default withholding of an undisclosable subject, and refusal of an institutional verb presented as attention
  witness cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh proves the native caller drops an undeclared verb and retains available-before-unavailable ordering after a large attention signal
  node_types Opportunity
  node_types StandingAddress
  owns Opportunity
  publishes Opportunity
  consumes InformationPolicy
  consumes FactDelta
  interacts information-policy
  interacts live-semantic-track
  internal_calculus the recommendation unit is an action against an addressed subject, so one subject may carry several opportunities and which is useful depends on the actor rather than on the object
  internal_calculus availability is a fact about the world and authority is a fact about the actor; an unavailable opportunity sinks below every available one regardless of relevance, because a sold-out thing is not an opportunity however well it matches
  internal_calculus each territory offers its own verbs -- life MEET/JOIN/GO/SAVE/HELP, live WATCH/JOIN/GO/FOLLOW, shop BUY/OFFER, work APPLY/APPROVE/CLAIM/FUND/CONTACT -- and a verb outside its territory is a category error rather than a low-ranking candidate
  internal_calculus disclosure runs before ranking, because offering an action on a subject an actor may not know exists discloses that subject
  invariant attention may reorder what is offered and may never open an obligation; the attention loop's invalidation envelope names only the standing address it reorders
  invariant the institutional loop is entered only by an enactment that produced an occurrence, never by somebody having looked
  invariant a standing address is recompiled rather than stored; an opportunity that outlived its world is the failure this shape exists to avoid
  forbidden_inference a ranked opportunity -> an authorized one (Authority still gates at effect time)
  forbidden_inference attention -> intent
  forbidden_inference an offered action -> an available one
  forbidden_inference a high rank -> a transaction being wanted (entertainment wins when entertainment is what the actor wants, and a ranker that pushed BUY upward because it is worth more would be optimizing for the estate)
  known_gap bf_standing_compile is now the native cheap ranking realization; SurfacePattern's newly authored CUE catalogue and territory verbs are not yet consumed by bf_standing_* at build time.
  known_gap relevance is supplied by the caller. Nothing here computes it from place, time, relationships or the live world, so this ranks honestly over scores it did not produce.
  known_gap the native caller ranks an explicit candidate input; PageComposition and SurfacePattern still need an owner-backed opportunity feed before this can become a public recommendation surface.
architecture surface-pattern
  canonical_name SurfacePattern
  family commons
  domain Commons / Surface grammar
  layer commons
  semantic_question What does this surface read, at what extent, and what may be done from it?
  purpose The reference UI estate as declared compiler targets rather than research notes, across all four territories. A pattern names the owner it reads, the extent it renders at, the action layer it carries, the authority that layer demands and the territory whose UX physics it belongs to -- so adding a surface is an authoring act and the borrowed behaviour of a familiar interface never brings its backend with it. Each reference project also records its licence and how this estate may use it, because donor and reference are a legal distinction rather than a preference.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/surface_pattern.json
  source_path schemas/control/surface-pattern.cue
  source_path schemas/control/standing-address.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/surface-pattern.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/surface_pattern.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/bounded_output.c
  node_types SurfacePattern
  node_types PatternCatalogue
  state_types chip
  state_types card
  state_types section
  state_types page
  state_types workspace
  owns SurfacePattern
  publishes SurfacePattern
  consumes Opportunity
  interacts surface-ir
  interacts standing-address-compiler
  internal_calculus extent decides the action layer: only page and workspace carry one, because a chip, card or section is a reference to a surface rather than the surface itself
  internal_calculus narrowing an extent drops the action layer and keeps the subject, so a workspace appearing elsewhere as a card is a projection rather than a second implementation
  internal_calculus lineage records which reference interface a pattern's behaviour was extracted from, which is what makes the claim that only the look was borrowed checkable rather than a slogan
  internal_calculus a reference project carries its licence and a use class; a copyleft or field-of-use licence cannot be marked a donor or an implementation, and the refusal names which obligation blocks it rather than reporting a generic denial
  internal_calculus a pattern belongs to exactly one territory and may only offer that territory's verbs, so a .live surface offering BUY is the same category error the opportunity model already refuses
  internal_calculus record_namespace is an optional descriptor-owned read boundary. It selects the CMS namespace of the owner being projected before URL slices run, so independently authored seed and compiled-census records with the same key never silently merge.
  invariant a pattern reads a CMS type or a native organ and the catalogue names which; a pattern reading both would be two patterns sharing a name whose human and machine projections could diverge unnoticed
  invariant a pattern carrying actions names the authority they require; an action layer that stated no requirement could not be refused by anything
  invariant record_namespace is authored by the descriptor and cannot be supplied by the URL; it narrows a truth owner but never names an actor, audience, entitlement or authority
  invariant a SurfacePattern query is assembled as complete bounded fragments and refused with 503 before SQLite prepare if its descriptor exceeds the query budget; a truncated query must not silently change the read set
  forbidden_inference a declared pattern -> a working or permitted one
  forbidden_inference a rendered action layer -> an authorized action (the pattern declares a requirement; AuthorityGraph decides at effect time)
  forbidden_inference a smaller extent -> a lesser subject
  forbidden_inference a familiar interface -> a familiar backend
  forbidden_inference a good interface -> a usable codebase (the licence decides, and an unrecognised licence is a reference until a person says otherwise)
  forbidden_inference matching record keys across namespaces -> one record or permission to merge them
  forbidden_inference a query-budget refusal -> no published records (the descriptor was not evaluated)
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/surface_pattern_contract_test.sh proves declared patterns render both human and machine projections, constrain slices and extent, refuse ambiguity and invalid controls, and keep a descriptor-owned namespace boundary from leaking an identically keyed seed row
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/surface-pattern.test.mjs tests all 31 prior Python contract cases against the CUE-authored catalogue, including extent narrowing, owner and authority refusal, all 41 patterns across four territories, and donor license classification
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/bounded_output_test.c proves an oversized fragment leaves the query buffer and offset unchanged, and a failed query writer refuses later appends
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/analysis/clean-compiler-offset.yml structurally rejects a new unchecked snprintf offset in the SurfacePattern compiler and shared subject renderers
  known_gap SurfacePattern is rendered natively but only the declared generic record grammar is lowered; richer renderer families still need to lower the same resolved descriptor into their own interaction grammars.

