architecture commerce-chain
  canonical_name CommerceChain
  family commons
  domain Commons / Commerce stages
  layer commons
  semantic_question Which of the fifteen distinct commerce facts has actually been established for this exchange?
  purpose Product, Listing, Inventory, AvailabilityObservation, Offer, Quote, Cart, Checkout, Commitment, Payment, Settlement, Fulfilment, Delivery, Satisfaction and Ownership are fifteen different facts that commerce systems routinely collapse into one row. A Shopify product, an eBay listing and a store two miles away having one are three different claims about the world, and a universal product row has already lost the ability to say which is true. Each stage names the owner that can establish it, because these collapse when a subsystem is asked a question it cannot answer.
  maturity measured
  source_path engine/core/src/commerce.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_commerce.h
  source_path schemas/control/commerce.yaff
  source_path schemas/control/commerce.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/commerce_chain.py.archive
  witness engine/core/tests/commerce_test.c tests all 225 stage pairs (the 210 distinct pairs plus fifteen identity checks), refuses a skipped delivery, retains commitment as the furthest stage with six further facts outstanding, and rejects an ownerless assertion
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_commerce_chain.py.archive
  node_types Stage
  state_types product
  state_types listing
  state_types inventory
  state_types availability_observation
  state_types offer
  state_types quote
  state_types cart
  state_types checkout
  state_types commitment
  state_types payment
  state_types settlement
  state_types fulfilment
  state_types delivery
  state_types satisfaction
  state_types ownership
  owns CommerceStage
  publishes CommerceStage
  interacts commitment-graph
  interacts money-graph
  internal_calculus each stage names the single owner that can establish it -- a catalogue cannot know whether anybody has one, a payment rail cannot know whether money settled, a courier cannot know whether the buyer wanted what arrived
  internal_calculus no stage may be skipped: recording one requires its predecessor, so an exchange reporting delivery with no fulfilment is refused rather than filed
  invariant the non-implication is checked over every pair rather than adjacent ones, because the dangerous collapses skip -- paid read as delivered, delivered read as owned
  forbidden_inference a listing -> a product in inventory
  forbidden_inference inventory -> availability here, now, to this buyer
  forbidden_inference an offer -> a quote priced for this buyer
  forbidden_inference a quote -> a reservation (the resource is not held)
  forbidden_inference a cart -> intent to buy
  forbidden_inference a checkout -> a commitment
  forbidden_inference a payment -> settled money
  forbidden_inference a settlement -> fulfilment
  forbidden_inference a delivery -> satisfaction
  forbidden_inference a delivery -> transferred ownership
  forbidden_inference satisfaction -> a discharged obligation (the buyer accepting is not the ledger closing)
  known_gap native C owns commerce_progress and the former Python implementation is archived because no live consumer remained; live UCP, Beckn, GS1 Digital Link and EPCIS bindings must call bf_commerce_record only after their own observations are admitted.
  known_gap the stages are recorded by callers and nothing yet drives them from UCP, Beckn, GS1 Digital Link or EPCIS observations, so the chain describes an exchange rather than following one.

architecture retention-gc
  canonical_name RetentionGC
  family commons
  domain Commons / Retention
  layer commons
  semantic_question May this record be removed now, and if not, who is keeping it?
  purpose The half of the retention lattice that acts. The lattice said which tier a record sits in and nothing removed anything, so it described what could be deleted by something that did not exist. This is that something: it removes what may go, refuses what may not, names who is holding whatever it refuses, and leaves a tombstone so that removing a body never denies the moment.
  maturity measured
  source_path engine/core/src/retention.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_retention.h
  source_path schemas/control/retention.yaff
  source_path schemas/control/retention.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/retention_gc.py.archive
  witness engine/core/tests/retention_test.c verifies the native shared-store owner: declared kind-to-tier selection, elapsed-clock collection, named holds, durable-floor refusal, tombstones without bodies, idempotent sweeps, and derived CommitmentGraph/EvidenceGraph holds that place and release only when their real source relation changes
  node_types RetainedRecord
  node_types Hold
  node_types Tombstone
  owns RetainedRecord
  owns Tombstone
  publishes Tombstone
  consumes LiveSemanticTrack
  interacts live-semantic-track
  interacts attention-cooling
  internal_calculus three conditions must all agree before a record is removed -- its tier is below the cooling floor, its tier's lifetime has elapsed, and nothing holds it; a tier at or above the floor has no lifetime at all and is never removed by time passing
  internal_calculus a hold names which owner is keeping the record (an open obligation, an evidence reference, a legal hold, or the person whose record it is) because a refusal that cannot say who is holding something cannot be acted on by anybody
  internal_calculus removal writes a tombstone carrying the occurrence, kind, tier and both timestamps and never the body, so material retention and institutional history are separable rather than one decision
  invariant an elapsed lifetime is permission to consider removal, never permission to remove; a hold outranks the clock
  invariant removing a record's body never denies that the moment happened, because a GC that deleted the fact along with the bytes would be enforcing amnesia rather than retention
  invariant a sweep is idempotent; running it twice removes nothing the second time
  forbidden_inference an elapsed lifetime -> permission to remove
  forbidden_inference a removed body -> the moment not having happened
  forbidden_inference a tombstone -> recoverable content
  forbidden_inference a released hold -> a record that was always removable
  known_gap native retention is bounded to BF_RETENTION_SWEEP_MAX records per transaction; a larger sweep must be explicitly paged rather than silently processing an unbounded set.
  known_gap obligation and evidence holds are now derived from their stores and lift when their reason ends; legal holds and user saves are still placed out of band by whoever has standing to place them, which is correct rather than missing.

interaction gc-removes-what-the-lattice-released
  source retention-gc
  destination live-semantic-track
  relation removes
  preserves the occurrence, kind, tier and timestamps of every removed record, as a tombstone
  preserves every record the lattice placed at or above the cooling floor, untouched by any amount of elapsed time
  drops the body of a removed record, permanently and without recovery
  forbidden_inference a removed body -> the moment not having happened
  forbidden_inference a tier below the floor -> a record that will be removed (a hold outranks the clock, and the holder is named)
  invalidates_on a hold is placed or released, or a kind's declared tier changes
  binding engine/core/src/retention.c

interaction holds-derive-from-their-owners
  source retention-gc
  destination commitment-graph
  relation derives_hold
  preserves which open obligations rest on a record, so a sweep cannot remove what a live promise depends on
  preserves the release: a terminal commitment stops justifying retention in the same pass that would have swept it
  drops the obligation's own content; retention needs to know that something is owed, not what
  forbidden_inference a derived hold -> a permanent one (it lifts when its reason ends)
  forbidden_inference a discharged commitment -> a removable record (another owner may still hold it)
  forbidden_inference a placed hold -> a record that was ever removable
  invalidates_on a commitment reaches or leaves a terminal state, or an obligation's record link changes
  binding engine/core/src/retention.c
  witness engine/core/tests/retention_test.c proves the half that matters is release rather than placement: a discharged commitment and retracted evidence relation lift their own native derived holds, while legal holds survive reconciliation untouched

interaction protocol-lowers-to-a-dependency-addressed-program
  source protocol-contract
  destination semantic-derivation
  relation compiles_to
  preserves each role as a read/write pair over exact parameter addresses, so a delta can be answered by intersection
  preserves the per-enactment address, so two runs of one contract hold two closures rather than one
  drops the role structure, the obligations and the authority requirements; the derivation graph needs addresses and edges and nothing about protocols
  forbidden_inference a FactDelta -> global invalidation
  forbidden_inference an invalidated role -> an invalidated enactment
  forbidden_inference a shared contract -> a shared closure
  forbidden_inference a written parameter -> a produced effect (a write is an address in a closure, not an occurrence)
  invalidates_on a role's requires or produces changes, or the contract stops conforming
  binding components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol-program.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/src/protocol_derivation_bridge.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/protocol_observation_bridge.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/protocol-observation.cue
  binding cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/protocol-observation.generated.json
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/protocol-program.test.mjs proves the invalidation is by intersection rather than by default: a delta on a parameter no role reads leaves every role valid, a delta mid-chain invalidates its reader and what depends on that reader's output while the roles upstream stay valid, and a delta naming one escrow parameter touches the escrow enactment and none of twenty concurrent quote-accepts. Every one of the twenty-one CUE library patterns lowers, and none is globally invalidated by an unrelated address (57 assertions)
  witness cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/protocol_derivation_bridge_test.c compiles against libbonfyre-fabric.a and proves two enactments register independent closures, invalidation stays enactment-scoped and target-specific, duplicate/nonconformant registration is atomic, and the emitted receipt is required by participation activation reporting
  witness cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/protocol_observation_bridge_test.c compiles the occurrence-scoped OGC API Common observation contract natively; cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/protocol_observation_bridge.test.mjs refuses an absent/tampered DomainProfile receipt or a native receipt for another occurrence, then records only compiled protocol state, never an enactment or an external effect
  witness cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/vectors/policy_compilation.json checks that the protocol runtime descriptor is exactly the CUE export, allowing the receipt hot path to omit a CUE subprocess without duplicating its law
  source_path cmd/BonfyreRetention/src/main.c
  internal_calculus a caller may not supply a tier; a kind carries its own closed retention tier, because a caller that could name the tier could delete anything by calling it short-lived
  internal_calculus a kind with no tier is refused rather than given a default lifetime, since a default would be a deletion policy nobody wrote
  witness 2026-09-19 the organ has a caller for the first time; it refuses `foreign_body` outright -- "this kind carries no retention tier" -- retains `chat` and then declines to remove it while its six-hour lifetime stands, and declines to remove `commerce` at all because an evidentiary tier is at the cooling floor where time cannot reach it
  known_gap the tier policy covers a conversation and clip domain -- reaction, presence, chat, utterance, speaker, topic, entity, place, chapter, clip_candidate, cta, claim, sponsor_mention, commerce -- and the estate's 449 MB of retained foreign source bodies match none of them, so nothing the estate actually retains can be registered with this organ at all
  known_gap the page organ composes from retained bodies, so a retention tier for them is not only a storage decision: removing a body removes the material a page is built from, and no tier has been written that accounts for that
  forbidden_inference a removed body -> the occurrence did not happen, or what it said was untrue

architecture foreign-live-ingest
  canonical_name ForeignLiveIngest
  family commons
  domain Commons / Foreign occurrence
  layer commons
  semantic_question What may this estate actually do with a live occurrence somebody else is hosting?
  purpose A creator who streams only elsewhere still produces an occurrence, and where rights permit its observable material can become a LiveSemanticTrack exactly like a native stream. That is what lets the estate understand a city before everybody in it streams natively. The difficulty is that being able to see something is four separate rights, and collapsing the first into the fourth is how an estate ends up redistributing somebody else's stream under its own name.
  maturity architectural
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/foreign-live.mjs
  source_path schemas/control/foreign-live.cue
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/foreign-live.test.mjs falsifies right implication, separate foreign provenance on native semantic events, independent claim corroboration, and observed-only occurrence filing over an in-memory SQLite spine
  node_types ForeignLiveSource
  state_types observable
  state_types retainable
  state_types derivable
  state_types republishable
  owns ForeignLiveSource
  publishes ForeignLiveSource
  consumes LiveSemanticTrack
  interacts live-semantic-track
  interacts foreign-twin
  interacts occurrence-origin
  internal_calculus the four rights are ordered and each is granted separately; a later right is meaningless without the earlier ones, and holding one never implies the next
  internal_calculus foreign material is mapped onto the native vocabulary rather than given a parallel one, so a caption is an utterance and a title is a topic and every downstream organ works unchanged
  internal_calculus every ingested event records the platform it came from, so a native and a foreign track are distinguishable per event and nothing downstream has to remember which it holds
  invariant a source granting nothing is not opened; an ingest that could be opened and then refused at every operation would report a capability the terms never gave
  invariant the asserter of an ingested claim is whoever spoke on the foreign stream, never the twin that observed it
  invariant every ingested occurrence is filed as OBSERVED; this estate did not cause a foreign stream and any other origin would let a later reader believe it did
  forbidden_inference observable -> retainable
  forbidden_inference retainable -> derivable
  forbidden_inference derivable -> republishable
  forbidden_inference an ingested claim -> a claim this estate is asserting
  forbidden_inference a foreign track -> a native one
  known_gap the Bun ingest now binds the CUE rights vocabulary, native LiveSemanticTrack, and the occurrence-origin SQLite relation; the rights grant is still supplied externally rather than established from platform terms.
  known_gap the rights are supplied by the caller as a declared grant with a basis string. Nothing yet derives them from a robots preflight, an API's terms or a licence, so the grant is honest about what it rests on and is not itself established here.
  known_gap downgraded from measured after review: the witness asserted this module's own declared constants rather than falsifying anything external, which is the maturity laundering this registry forbids. Source and witness lines removed until a test exists that could fail for a reason the module did not author.

architecture protocol-density-law
  canonical_name ProtocolDensityLaw
  family commons
  domain Commons / Protocol
  layer law
  semantic_question Does this protocol integration add a relation the machine did not have, without taking ownership of a fact something else already owns?
  purpose The rule that stops a protocol estate becoming a taxonomy swamp. Seven hundred and thirty-nine protocols are not seven hundred and thirty-nine integrations; they are a library of typed transition grammars, and a new one earns its place only by adding a relation and not a truth store. Written as an architecture so it can be cited and failed against, rather than as advice.
  maturity architectural
  source_path architecture/commons/protocol-commons.yaff
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/participation_report.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/quote-capture.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/economic-reports.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/contract-drive.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/enact-drive.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/read-protocol-contract.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/read_protocol_drive.test.mjs invokes both default shells with real native Lex and mocked Facet, preserves DESCRIBE then QUERY then DISCOVER selection, refuses non-read/domain-derived facets and option-like owner arguments, distinguishes compiler failure from malformed output, and requires attempted successful transport and matching body digest before an enact call; no external effects are executed
  known_gap native enact still accepts no receipt and does not bind the original observer identity; ACTOR is a caller assertion, retained allow is not current permission, and DB plus evidence-file writes are not one transaction. The Bun retirement does not claim these native boundaries are closed.
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/economic_reports.test.mjs exercises the actual quote-capture shell through bounded Bun retained-file reads, recovers payment-required envelopes from prose bodies, preserves body/header and quote digests, atomically publishes zero-spend quoted receipts, and refuses malformed or oversized inputs without replacing prior output; no fetch, payment or carrier verification occurs
  consumes ProtocolContract
  consumes EvidenceGraph
  publishes ProtocolFacetContract
  internal_calculus a facet is admitted only if it adds at least one previously unavailable relation from the finite set: DISCOVER, IDENTIFY, AUTHENTICATE, AUTHORIZE, OBSERVE, SYNCHRONIZE, DESCRIBE, QUERY, FILTER, SUBSCRIBE, NOTIFY, TRANSFER, STREAM, PUBLISH, FEDERATE, TASK, COMMAND, NEGOTIATE, QUOTE, COMMIT, PAY, SETTLE, PROVE, VERIFY, ROUND_TRIP
  internal_calculus compile facets from the phenotype of the thing crossing the fabric rather than from its domain; one object may carry several phenotypes at once, and a domain-keyed compiler degenerates into `if earthquake then FDSN`
  internal_calculus the ladder is five distinct states and collapsing any adjacent pair is the failure mode: a candidate protocol match is not a compiled ProtocolContract, which is not a ProtocolEnactment, which is not obligations closed, which is not an authorized effect
  invariant a protocol adds a relation and never acquires ownership of a fact already owned elsewhere; seventeen projections of one earthquake are seventeen carriers over one typed closure and not seventeen earthquakes
  invariant every owner handoff leaves occurrence-keyed evidence, because a handoff that leaves none is a handoff nobody can measure and a running chain reports as depth zero
  invariant density is measured as branching and rejoining over one occurrence, not as the longest path; a straight line of eight owners is not denser than six branches that rejoin
  invariant a source-native carrier and a Bonfyre projection carrier are different facts about different hops; SeedLink is what a seismic source speaks and MOQT is how this estate may deliver an addressed object, and neither substitutes for the other
  cannot_infer a protocol answering -> the interaction being lawful on this subject for this actor
  cannot_infer a richer representation -> a more authoritative fact; QuakeML beside GeoJSON is more seismology and not more authority
  cannot_infer a matching digest or a valid signature -> source truth; RFC 9530 and RFC 9421 carry integrity and communication authenticity, neither of which is correctness or permission to redistribute
  cannot_infer robots permitting a read -> a licence to republish; an observation right and a rights profile are separate facts
  cannot_infer a conditional 304 -> the thing not having changed in the world; it says the representation this estate holds is still current
  cannot_infer a subscription notification -> an observation; a notice is a dirty signal and the source is reread through the admission law
  cannot_infer a model-derived estimate -> an observed measurement; a PAGER fatality estimate never flattens into observed fatalities
  cannot_infer an alert-shaped projection -> authority to warn; CAP sits after AuthorityGraph and a red impact estimate is not permission to issue anything
  cannot_infer public source bytes -> something this estate may charge for; a price may attach to admitted analysis this estate added, never to the observation it read
  source_path schemas/control/owner-participation.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/participation_test.sh
  internal_calculus an owner reports participation as a row carrying the digest of what it read and the digest of what it produced. Neither is decoration: a reader that accepts an axis, an owner and a state at face value lets any owner write itself onto any rung, and the reader did exactly that -- it ended in `return raw`, so a document claiming economic/settled was counted as a settlement
  internal_calculus the axes are declared with their rungs in one place and the reader refuses a state that is not a rung of its own axis, so a new owner can report without a new reader and cannot invent a ladder for itself
  invariant an owner emits the lowest rung it actually earned and never one above it; the address plane emits discovery/routable because it can form the address, and refuses capability/eligible because eligibility needs a lowerer that survives an exact cut
  invariant a rung that requires something this estate cannot grant itself is not emitted from local compilation. semantic/carrier_conformant outranks profile_bound, which requires a retained body, so deriving conformance from declared metadata would launder a rung above one that needs real evidence
  cannot_infer six axes measured -> six axes deep; every one of them is at its lowest rung, and the estate reports longest_owner_path 2 with rejoin_points 0, which is a tree and not yet a braid
  cannot_infer an occurrence at depth 1 -> an occurrence that was reached; depth 1 means one owner left checkable evidence about it, and for 4,890 of them that owner read a description rather than a source
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/participation_test.sh runs on every build and proves the refusals rather than the acceptances: a row claiming economic/settled with short digests, a row naming a state that is not a rung of its axis, and a bare row with no schema are each read and none is counted
  source_path schemas/control/application-kind-facts.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/grammar_density_test.sh
  internal_calculus density is relations carried and never names declared. This estate holds thirty string-union grammars and four hundred and thirteen members; fifty-eight of those members appear nowhere but their own declaration, and the widest grammar, #ApplicationKind, had forty-three of fifty-nine dead
  internal_calculus a grammar earns density by binding to another grammar, not by growing. #ApplicationKind named fifty-nine applications and carried nothing, so the facet compiler -- which types four thousand external occurrences and derives twenty-five relations from their phenotypes -- could not see a single site application. Binding each kind to the phenotypes it is makes the relations follow instead of being restated per capability program
  internal_calculus a kind carries several phenotypes because a thing is often more than one. A Marketplace is an economic offer and a dataset; a Podcast is a media asset and a versioned record. The compiler already types occurrences with several at once and the binding matches it rather than forcing a single answer
  invariant the phenotype relation table is emitted by its owner and never re-parsed. It lived only as a multi-line C initialiser, and a line-indexed parse of a table whose rows wrap attributes one phenotype's relations to another -- it reported that a Checkout admits VERIFY and not PAY, which is neither true nor what the table says
  invariant a binding names only phenotypes the compiler holds; a grammar that binds to a phenotype nothing implements is two vocabularies wearing one name
  cannot_infer an admitted relation -> a lawful one; admission is what the phenotype can carry and AuthorityGraph decides what may be done with it
  cannot_infer a bound application kind -> a built application; the binding says what a kind is, not that anything realizes it
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/grammar_density_test.sh runs on every build: every declared kind bound, no binding for an undeclared kind, every phenotype and extent exercised rather than a few carrying all of it, and every kind admitting at least one relation
  witness fifty-nine application kinds went from zero derivable relations to seven hundred and sixty-six, a mean of thirteen each, reaching all twenty-five relation kinds
  source_path schemas/control/content-type-facts.cue
  internal_calculus the estate's own rows enter the relation grammar the same way external ones do. The facet compiler typed 4,891 external occurrences and none of the 54 content types carrying the institution's own data, so it could propose relations for the outside world and nothing for the inside: a media_program could not be known to be a media asset, a pack_demand could not be known to be an obligation
  internal_calculus the estate is no longer one thing and the grammar says so. Twelve domains -- pack, music, media, community, site, surface, external, spatial, governance, contract, frappe, cms -- are separate bodies of meaning over one relation spine, which is what lets a question be asked across them rather than inside one of them
  invariant COMMAND is reachable from application kinds and not from content types, because COMMANDABLE_RESOURCE is a device phenotype and nothing the CMS holds is a device. The witness asserts this rather than assuming it, so a content type that ever claims COMMAND has to justify holding a commandable row
  invariant neither grammar has to reach every relation alone; together they must. Site applications reach all twenty-five and authored rows reach twenty-four, and the pair is what the estate can actually derive
  cannot_infer a declared phenotype -> a row that exists; several content types carry no rows at all and the binding says what a type is rather than that anything was written into it
  witness the density witness covers both grammars on every build: 59 application kinds and 54 content types across 12 domains, 1,463 relations derivable, all 25 relation kinds reached
  known_gap the household audience is bound by no application kind and no content type. Either something household-scoped is unwritten, or that audience belongs to a body other than a site application or an authored row
  source_path schemas/control/standing-action-facts.cue
  internal_calculus three vocabularies described the affordance and nothing checked they agreed: the forty-four #ExternalAffordance declares, the thirty-eight the compiler mapped to relations, and the thirty-eight the estate's data carries. Six were declared and mapped to nothing, so a source arriving with SHIP would have contributed nothing to its own facet set and no one would have been told
  internal_calculus the fourth law is mechanical where it belongs. #StandingAction names twenty-eight things a person does and was read by nothing at all; binding it says which six computation may carry to completion and which twenty-two are a commitment no engine may close on someone's behalf
  invariant data stays inside its grammar. The witness refuses an affordance the data carries that #ExternalAffordance does not declare, and an affordance the compiler maps that nothing declares
  invariant anything that moves money, grants authority or discloses is a commitment. BUY, SELL, FUND, APPROVE, APPLY, SHARE, ESCALATE and JOIN are asserted rather than left to drafting care, because an engine that could close them on a person's behalf is what the fourth law exists to prevent
  cannot_infer a satisfiable requirement -> a permitted action; the relations say what the machine must be able to do for the action to be possible at all, and AuthorityGraph still decides whether this actor may
  witness the density witness now covers four grammars on every build: 59 application kinds, 54 content types across 12 domains, 44 affordances all mapped in three agreeing vocabularies, and 28 standing actions split six reachable to twenty-two at the human line
  witness 2026-10-10: the estate had grown to 99 content types with rows and only 57 declared, so the density witness failed on 42 of them. All 42 are now declared in schemas/control/content-type-facts.cue with a household domain added, each given the narrower phenotype where it records something observed, declared or held: an observed offer is filed under external, a role, a need and a requirement are documents and not obligations or capabilities, a session or presence is a recorded event and not a live entity. Density witness: 59 kinds + 99 content types across 13 domains, 2013 relations derivable, all 25 reached; reader agreement and the native witness pass
  internal_calculus a bound grammar is a description until a protocol can carry it. Ability is the protocol: 739 of them each offer some subset of the twenty-five relations, and a grammar member is executable exactly to the degree that one of them offers what its phenotype admits. `reach` answers this for a phenotype set, which is what a bound grammar has, because `compile` answers it only for an occurrence and an application kind is not an occurrence and never will be
  invariant every grammar member is servable by at least one protocol. All 141 members across the three bound grammars are, with a range of 310 to 730 protocols each; a member no protocol can serve is a name that cannot be executed however well it is typed
  witness the protocol census over 739 protocols: QUERY 413, OBSERVE 358, FILTER 240, TRANSFER 213 at the abundant end, and PROVE 14, ROUND_TRIP 14, SETTLE 16, SYNCHRONIZE 31, VERIFY 35 at the scarce end
  known_gap the machine-readable internet offers reading in abundance and proof almost not at all. The four scarcest relations -- PROVE, ROUND_TRIP, SETTLE, VERIFY -- are exactly the four that turn an observation into a settled and verified fact, and that shape explains this estate's own numbers rather than excusing them: 3,316 observations, 2,344 reads enacted, nothing settled. It is a fact about the corpus and not a defect here, and the witness asserts the scarcity so a change that appears to make proof abundant is looked at rather than believed
  internal_calculus how many grammars are bound is answered from cue's own normalised definition and not from the source text. Two regex attempts over the schemas gave two different wrong answers: the first called ExternalAffordance and RelationKind bare, which are the two most bound things here, and the second missed every list element type because it required a colon or a space before the reference where the text has a bracket or a dot
  invariant a vocabulary declared twice is compared twice. The axis set is declared as #AddressAxis and again inside the #AddressTerm pattern, and only the pattern was ever compared with the native plane; all three agree at sixty-eight and the witness now checks all three rather than two
  witness the measured answer: thirty-one string-union grammars, twenty-nine used inside CUE structures, and two -- AddressAffordance and AddressAxis -- used only from C, where both have real tables. None is genuinely unbound
  known_gap an earlier note in this entry claimed twenty-six of thirty grammars were unbound. That figure was never measured and is wrong by the width of the claim. CandidateKind is mirrored in C with a witness proving the two sets identical, ExpectedPredicateState is mapped by nativeOwnerPredicateGrammar through owner, opcode and native state, and AddressAffordance is carried by PHENOTYPE_AFFORDANCE. The retraction is kept here because the number was reported before it was checked
  known_gap SHIP, STORE, CONTROL, RESERVE, FINANCE and NOTIFY are mapped and carried by no occurrence in the estate. The mapping is a prepared answer rather than a measured one, and the first source that carries one will be the first test of it
  known_gap the law is stated and only partly enforced. The relation vocabulary is not yet a validated field on a ProtocolFacetContract, so nothing refuses a facet that adds no relation; participation_report measures the ladder and does not gate on it.
  internal_calculus a ForeignTwin receipt is the ExternalEstate handoff and never says so, because the observer records what it saw rather than who handed it the occurrence. Both readers of the evidence must synthesise that edge or neither may; one did and one did not, and the estate's own first hop was absent from every density report it had produced
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/reader_agreement_test.sh runs on every build and holds the two readers to one owner graph over one evidence file: the participation reader and the density reader must agree on the edge count, the longest path and which axes an occurrence reached
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/enact-drive.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/quote-capture.sh
  internal_calculus the rungs above contract_compiled were called unreachable because each needs an actor, an authority or money, and all three existed the whole time pointed at nothing. The one interaction this estate has actually performed is a read, and a read has all three: the actor is the identity the source was shown, the authority is the source's own robots rule, and the money is nothing because a permitted GET of a public representation costs nothing
  internal_calculus a contract is compiled for the relation that was performed and not for the first one the compiler proposes. Taking the first shape-derived facet produced AUTHENTICATE contracts against a thousand sources nobody authenticated to and PUBLISH contracts against sources whose own receipt says robots allowing a read is not a licence to republish
  internal_calculus phenotype has a third derivation tier and it is the only one that rests on bytes. Shape reads what a thing is described as and domain reads the neighbourhood it sits in; both were available before anything was fetched and both are guesses. A carrier detected in a retained body is the source saying what it is, and 451 of 519 conformant occurrences were typed by observation after the catalogue had typed them otherwise
  internal_calculus a price is not a payment. Three sources answered the sweep with HTTP 402 and an x402 envelope, which is a published price, and reading it cost nothing. quoted is rung one of five and committed, paid, settled and reconciled all remain unreached because all four move money
  invariant no authority is granted by this estate to itself to reach a rung. The read relation reports authority_required false, so the flag that would grant one is not passed and cannot be the reason anything closes
  invariant a rung is reached only where the evidence still holds at the moment it is claimed: robots allowed, the fetch returned 200, and the retained bytes still hash to what the receipt recorded. A body that has drifted from its receipt is skipped rather than enacted on a weaker basis
  cannot_infer an enacted read -> a licence to republish or derive, or authority over anything else that source offers
  cannot_infer obligations_closed -> the source agreeing that they were; the obligations of a permitted read were discharged at request time and this records that, it does not negotiate it
  cannot_infer a quote -> an intention to pay, a budget, or a fair price
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tools/enact-drive.sh enacted 2,338 reads under published permission with zero spend, and refused 835 that were not permitted or never fetched
  known_gap the braid branches and does not rejoin. branch_points is 1 and rejoin_points is 0, because every rung that would join two owners into a third needs an observation, an authority or a price. The rejoin is not missing work; it is work that cannot be done without leaving this machine.
  known_gap the economic axis has five declared rungs and three quotes. The earlier reading -- that a quote needs a price from a carrier this estate does not hold -- was true of the carriers and false of the sources: three answered with HTTP 402 and a published price. The other four rungs move money and remain unreached, which is a decision and not a limitation.
  known_gap 146 facts are produced by an architecture nothing consumes and 55 are consumed by an architecture nothing produces. Those pairs are where the rejoin would come from, and until they are closed the estate is a set of owners that each report separately rather than a machine that hands work along.
  known_gap phenotype compilation is described and unbuilt. Facets are still authored per protocol family rather than selected from the phenotypes an occurrence carries, so the abstraction jump this entry names has not been taken.

architecture protocol-facet-compiler
  canonical_name ProtocolFacetCompiler
  family commons
  domain Commons / Protocol
  layer compiler
  semantic_question Given what this occurrence is, which protocols could lawfully add a relation to it that the machine does not already have?
  purpose The abstraction jump ProtocolDensityLaw named and did not take. Facets compile from the phenotype of the thing crossing the fabric rather than from its domain, so 739 protocols stop being 739 integrations and become a library of typed transition grammars. One object carries several phenotypes at once and each opens different lawful facets.
  maturity measured
  source_path schemas/control/protocol-facet.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFacet/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/src/protocol_derivation_bridge.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/participation_report.mjs
  consumes ExternalEstateIndex
  consumes ProtocolContract
  publishes ProtocolFacetContract
  internal_calculus a facet is the intersection of three things: a phenotype the occurrence carries, a relation the protocol offers, and that relation being meaningful for that phenotype. Drop the phenotype and this is domain matching; drop the protocol's own offer and it invents capability; drop the meaningfulness table and a payment protocol acquires a relation over a weather field
  internal_calculus phenotypes are derived from evidence the corpus already carries and already witnesses -- candidate affordances, estate roles, topic domains, the spatial classification -- rather than from a fresh reading of the same descriptions, which would be a second opinion with no extra evidence behind it
  internal_calculus evidence comes in two tiers and they are never merged. Shape evidence is an affordance or role that names what the thing is and is sufficient alone. Domain evidence says what a domain is mostly made of -- a deed, a permit, a policy and an invoice are versioned records, so law, government, housing and finance carry VERSIONED_RECORD -- and is weaker, so every facet records which tier admitted it
  internal_calculus a facet names the protocol families its phenotype is usually carried over, so it says which relation is possible and over what; AddressPlane still addresses affordances and never protocol names
  internal_calculus invalidation is per phenotype because density is only affordable if it is precise: a moving thing is invalidated by moving and not by a price changing, and more protocol projections must not mean more recomputation
  internal_calculus AddressPlane coordinates for a facet are affordances and never protocol names; a live bus and a private physiological reading share temporal:live and are separated by InformationPolicy and Authority rather than by routing vocabulary
  invariant the relation and phenotype vocabularies are finite and declared once in CUE; the compiler's own lists are compared against that declaration, because two independently maintained copies is how a finite vocabulary stops being finite
  invariant a compiled facet claims candidate_match and nothing higher unless something witnesses the next rung; promotion to contract_compiled requires the facet to be one this compiler would emit, a ForeignTwin receipt for that exact occurrence whose body still hashes to it, and a registration performed by the native ProtocolContract owner
  invariant the program count on a compiled contract is what the native registrar returned and never a number chosen by the promoter
  invariant a protocol binding carries the digest of the domain binding under it and the domain binding carries the digest of the receipt under that; a contract with nothing beneath it does not verify
  invariant a contract's shape follows its relation; describer/compiler/reader is lawful for a read and wrong for anything that changes something, so COMMAND, TASK, COMMIT, PAY, SETTLE, AUTHORIZE, PUBLISH, TRANSFER and FEDERATE construct an authority-bearing acting role and a read does not
  invariant an obligation is opened only where the relation creates one, so closing has something real to discharge rather than nothing
  invariant obligations and evidence are separate axes and neither is rounded up; an exchange is reported closed only when its obligations are terminal and its required claims presently stand
  invariant granting authority is an institutional act and is never implied by asking to enact; without a grant the authorize step refuses and names the role that lacks the permission
  invariant discharging an obligation is an act someone performs; recording is never delivery, so enactment does not discharge and closure is unreachable without it
  invariant domain evidence may carry a candidate facet and may not carry a compiled contract on its own; a contract asserts a shape for this source rather than for sources like it, and an override is recorded on the binding so the weaker basis stays visible
  invariant the phenotype that admitted a relation is resolved the same way everywhere, preferring shape evidence; two answers to which phenotype admitted a facet would make the derivation tier meaningless
  invariant a facet defers to the owner of every fact it touches and acquires none of them; it names those owners rather than implying them
  invariant only affordances that say what a thing is may derive a phenotype; an affordance describing how a source is reached says nothing about its shape
  invariant a facet names the phenotype that admitted it and the tier that evidence came from; a facet that cannot is a domain match wearing a phenotype label
  invariant acceptance is every domain the corpus carries, not a favourable specimen per domain; a domain that compiles nothing must be visible in the report rather than omitted from it
  invariant this compiler plans observations and never performs one; it says which occurrence is worth a request and ForeignTwin decides robots, retains bytes and writes the receipt
  cannot_infer a candidate facet -> a compiled contract, an enactment, closed obligations, or an authorized effect
  cannot_infer a protocol offering a relation -> that protocol being reachable, admitted, or lawful on this subject for this actor
  cannot_infer 7.1 million candidate facets -> 7.1 million available interactions; this is candidate adjacency across the estate and realized participation is measured separately and is far smaller
  cannot_infer a phenotype -> an observation; a phenotype is a shape read off a description and no position, measurement or record follows from it
  cannot_infer a phenotype distribution of zero -> the phenotype being wrong; this corpus carries no evidence shaped like it, which is a fact about the corpus
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh holds the compiler to the declaration and to the ladder: its 25 relations and 15 phenotypes are compared byte for byte against schemas/control/protocol-facet.cue, no protocol name appears in any AddressPlane coordinate, an OccurrenceBraidInput declares actor context and authority cut absent rather than defaulting them, every compiled facet is candidate_match and validates against #ProtocolFacetContract, every facet defers to ForeignTwin and AuthorityGraph and names what invalidates it, an earthquake feed is never offered COMMAND whatever a protocol claims, and a corpus that cannot be read fails rather than reporting an empty estate (36 assertions)
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh measures full depth across the estate: 4,891 occurrences against the 739 protocol occurrences among them yield 7,124,689 candidate facets in about 0.3 s, with all 15 phenotypes and all 25 relations present in the distribution so an unpopulated one is visible rather than absent
  known_gap phenotype derivation inherits the precision of the affordance layer beneath it. EVENT reaches only 132 occurrences because the corpus assigns ALERT and REPORT sparsely, which is why the USGS earthquake feed is a DATASET and a SPATIAL_RESOURCE and not an EVENT; hand-correcting that one source would be the `if earthquake then FDSN` failure wearing the opposite coat.
  known_gap SUPPLY_CHAIN_OBJECT derives from nothing. Its candidate signals were measured as false positives and removed, and no estate role names the shape, so the phenotype is declared and unpopulated.
  known_gap a facet carries no carrier candidates and no representation requirements. Both fields exist in the contract and the compiler leaves them empty, so a facet says which relation is possible and not yet over what carrier or in which representation.
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves the generalization spans the machine rather than one specimen: all 61 topic domains the corpus carries compile candidate facets, every domain the brief names across mobility, energy, manufacturing, medicine, finance, media, research, buildings, law, food, telecommunications, computing and retail among them, the larger domains exercise all 15 phenotypes and all 25 relations, and no phenotype or relation in the vocabulary is left at zero across the estate
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves a facet is carried and invalidated precisely: a LIVE_ENTITY facet names GTFS-RT, SIRI, FIXM, AIS, MOQT and MQTT as carriers, is invalidated by position and trip changes, and is not invalidated by a price change; every facet names the phenotype that admitted it and whether that came from shape or from domain evidence; and the shape tier is a subset of the total so a merged report cannot hide which evidence did the work
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh measures the estate at full depth: 4,891 occurrences against the 739 protocol occurrences among them compile 10,327,712 candidate facets in about 0.4 s, with 4,880 of 4,891 carrying at least one phenotype and all 61 domains represented
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves the rung and the three refusals that give it meaning: a promotion emits a domain binding then a protocol binding with a verifying digest chain from receipt to semantic record to domain binding to native registration receipt; a relation the phenotype does not admit is refused; a receipt observing a different occurrence cannot be borrowed; and a body that has drifted from its receipt compiles nothing
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves the rung is not a specimen: two occurrences in different domains compile differently named contracts through the same code path, each naming the phenotype that admitted it and the evidence tier that phenotype came from
  witness cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tools/participation_report.mjs measures ten occurrences across ten domains -- buildings, energy, finance, food, law, manufacturing, medicine, research, telecommunications and vehicles -- at braid_depth 3 over ExternalEstate to ForeignTwin to DomainProfile to ProtocolContract, against a prior estate in which exactly one occurrence could reach 3 because the report required the contract to be literally ogc-api-common-observation with exactly three programs
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves the whole ladder is produced by the owner that owns each rung: authorize refuses and names the role lacking the permission until an AuthorityGraph grant exists, bf_protocol_contract_enact_authorized opens the obligation the relation creates, evidence standing alone leaves it outstanding, discharging alone leaves it outstanding, and only both together reach obligations_closed through bf_protocol_contract_close
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves the contract shape follows the relation: every read facet carries no authority requirement and every facet whose relation changes something carries one, and each names the representations its phenotype is carried in
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves domain evidence cannot carry a contract alone: a relation admitted only by a domain-tier phenotype is refused, the same promotion succeeds when the weaker basis is named, and the binding records that it was domain evidence
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh proves interpretation is not observation: 4,880 occurrences receive occurrence-keyed semantic evidence at the interpreted rung, none claims profile_bound, none claims the observation axis, and an occurrence with no phenotype is left alone rather than given an empty one
  known_gap effect_authorized is an AuthorityGraph grant this estate wrote for itself. Nothing external has delegated any of these permissions, so the rung proves the gate works and not that anyone outside has authorized anything.
  witness cmd/BonfyreFacet/tests/facet_test.sh compiles an observation plan over the whole corpus: 4,891 occurrences carrying an http(s) address, grouped by host so a driver can pace itself per host without sorting, and ordered within a host by how many candidate facets each would unlock so a partial sweep spends its requests where they matter
  known_gap the plan orders by candidate facets, which is a measure of what this estate would gain and not of what a source wants. A source that publishes reluctantly and a source that publishes generously sort the same way.
  known_gap the eleven occurrences this compiler cannot type carry no facets and therefore sort last, which is the wrong end: they are the ones an observation would teach the most about. Ordering cannot fix it, because phenotypes are read from the corpus description rather than from an observed body, so observing them changes nothing until a DomainProfile reads the bytes.
  known_gap eleven occurrences carry no phenotype at all and stay at depth zero. Their descriptions name a shape this compiler cannot read, which is a fact about those eleven descriptions.
  known_gap density reads explicit from_owner and to_owner pairs and does not reimplement the participation report's schema-specific normalizer; a receipt that only carries a twin_id contributes no edge here. Two normalizers would be two opinions, so the gap is recorded rather than closed by duplication.

architecture text-extraction-rules
  canonical_name TextExtractionRules
  family commons
  domain Commons / Text
  layer law
  semantic_question Where in this document is that value, and who decided the answer?
  purpose The rule that stops every call site inventing a parser. This estate had 163 hand-rolled field extractors in C and 49 grep, sed and awk extractions across its witnesses, each written at the moment it was needed by someone thinking about something else. Two were wrong in ways nothing could notice, and both were the same wrongness: an undeclared text rule failing quietly.
  maturity measured
  source_path schemas/control/text-rules.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreLex/src/bf_lex.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreLex/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreLex/tests/lex_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreLex/tests/bf_lex_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/source_depth_projection.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  consumes ForeignTwinGraph
  publishes ExtractionRule
  internal_calculus one implementation per field kind and no more: a JSON string with its escaping, a JSON scalar as written, an HTTP header matched case-insensitively, one relation out of a multi-relation Link header, a tab column, a whitespace-separated report column, an indented yaff field, a percent-decoded query parameter, a command-line flag. A call site names a ruleset and a field and never a key, an escaping rule or a document shape
  internal_calculus writing is a field kind too. Nineteen copies of the JSON emitter held sixteen different opinions about escaping, and reading them back was never the check on them; one document per binary was simply assumed well-formed
  internal_calculus a key is addressed at the depth it is written, and a path addresses it exactly: session.token is the token of the session rather than whichever token the document happens to carry first. A flat search finds a key at any depth and inside any value, which is how a record was selected by an address nested in its own profile
  internal_calculus a document is a sequence of records whether it is written one per line or all on one, so selecting a record by one of its fields and reading another is a declared shape rather than a substitution spanning a line
  internal_calculus the vocabulary lives in CUE and is exported rather than restated in C; a second copy would be a second vocabulary, which is the thing being fixed
  internal_calculus a receipt file is a log, so a ruleset can be read at its newest line rather than its oldest; reading the oldest is how a superseded validator kept being handed back to sources
  invariant absent, present-and-empty, and present are three different answers and are never collapsed; a missing required field fails loudly rather than yielding an empty string that reads like a legitimate value
  invariant a value too long for its buffer is reported as too long and never as absent; testing capacity before the closing quote reported a 64-character digest missing, which read as a receipt with no digest
  invariant a request for a field nobody declared lists what is declared rather than returning empty; an extractor that answers questions it was never given a rule for is guessing
  invariant undeclared keys in a document are reported and never discarded in silence
  invariant a control character never reaches a document unescaped and never disappears from one; a writer that drops a newline has edited the content, not the encoding
  invariant a bounded escape truncates before an escape sequence and never through one; a document cut mid-\u is a document nothing can read
  invariant what this estate writes, this estate can read back: the emitter and the reader are exercised against each other on the same awkward bytes rather than each being assumed correct alone
  invariant shared HTML text emission writes ordinary spans at once and escapes ampersand, angle brackets, and both quote styles; WebAddress does not emit each ordinary byte through a separate stdio call
  cannot_infer an undeclared key -> a key that should not exist; it is a key nobody wrote a rule for, and whether the fix is a rule or a rename is not something the reader can tell
  cannot_infer a document with no missing required fields -> a well-formed document; the check knows the fields it was told about
  cannot_infer a declared ruleset -> the document conforming to the schema it names; the ruleset says where to look and not what is true
  cannot_infer one shared reader -> one correct reader; it means disagreement is now a single decision that can be examined, and a decision made once can still be made wrongly
  cannot_infer a converted call site -> a call site whose caller wanted what the shared implementation does; three witnesses were converted and immediately failed, which is how their silent emptiness was found rather than a sign the conversion was safe
  witness cmd/BonfyreLex/tests/lex_test.sh proves the two failures that motivated this are closed by construction: an ETag containing escaped quotes reads back whole, a 64-character digest in a 65-byte buffer reads as a value rather than an absence, a receipt log can be read at its newest line, a redirect chain's final header block wins over an earlier one, an empty trailing tab column is present and empty, a request for an undeclared field lists the declared ones, and a document carrying keys nobody declared reports them by name (31 assertions)
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/http_envelope_test.sh exercises the shared reader in its first real caller: ForeignTwin's receipt reader is now bf_lex and conditional re-observation returns 304 and repeat_observed against a live source
  witness cmd/BonfyreLex/tests/bf_lex_test.c holds 84 assertions, including a shared HTML emission check for both attribute quote styles alongside the JSON, receipt, and query reader cases
  witness make all builds 111 of 112 binaries and runs each organ's own witnesses; the one failure is an unrelated generated symbol another agent has not emitted yet. The conversion is exercised by whatever each organ already proves rather than by a claim about it
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/auth_surface_test.sh passes on a real user id. It read a fixed-width report table with a JSON substitution, which matched nothing; sed exited 0, the variable was empty, and the witness asserted on the empty string and passed for as long as it had existed
  known_gap four rulesets are declared and the estate has many more shapes. The duplication is closed: 48 C sources and 7 witnesses reach 137 call sites through the one implementation, and the estate's other shared reader, bf_json_str with 47 callers, delegates to it rather than disagreeing with it.
  known_gap three readers are deliberately not converted. BonfyreAuth's json_field is stricter than the shared one on purpose -- it refuses an unknown escape, a control byte and an empty value, because it is reading a credential rather than a document. BonfyreWebAddress's studio_json_string carries a JSON path and a form-encoded fallback in one function and another agent is working in that file. BonfyreFPQ's legacy_from_10code tree is excluded from the build entirely. All three are named here rather than left unmentioned.
  known_gap array iteration is not a declared shape. BonfyreGraph walks an array of objects and BonfyreVec scans a list of ids, both by hand, because bf_lex addresses a field and a record and not yet a sequence.
  known_gap two writers remain and both are deliberate. BonfyreBitNet accumulates into its own buffer rather than writing to a stream, and BonfyreTranscriptClean and BonfyreBrief unescape lossily on purpose -- a transcript wants a newline as a space, not as \n. Neither is the shared shape, and declaring them as one would be the laundering this file exists to prevent.
  known_gap the rules declare where a field is and the emitters declare how a value is written, and nothing yet declares which documents this estate produces. `check` can say a document carries an undeclared key; it cannot say a binary emitted a document no ruleset describes.
  known_gap the atlas reports the field keys it stores and never reads and does not refuse them. Refusing would fail CI on 272 lines authors already wrote, so the loss is now visible and still present.

architecture marketplace-observation
  canonical_name MarketplaceObservation
  family commons
  domain Commerce / Observed marketplace material
  layer material
  semantic_question What does observing a marketplace feed entitle this estate to say about an exchange, and what does it not?
  purpose Reads shopping feeds as commerce rather than as news. A marketplace lot becomes an exchange on the fifteen-stage chain, with exactly the two stages an observation establishes, and the thirteen it does not shown with the party who alone could establish each.
  maturity implemented
  node_types MarketplaceLot
  node_types ObservedExchange
  edge_types establishes
  edge_types outstanding_on
  internal_calculus a lot is told from an article by its address: a marketplace reserves a path for lots, and editorial in the same feed is not a lot whatever it is called
  internal_calculus an observation establishes product and listing and nothing further; inventory belongs to the merchant's system of record, availability to a receipted observation, offer and quote to the merchant, and everything past checkout to the buyer, the rails and the carrier
  internal_calculus the thirteen unestablished stages are the honest answer to what can be done here -- not a button this estate owns, but the next fact and the party entitled to establish it
  invariant stages are recorded through the commerce organ, which requires exactly the prior stage, so no projection can invent a transitive completion
  invariant a price this estate has not observed is shown as not observed, never as zero and never as the merchant's asking price
  invariant every dated lot is materialized once through BonfyreCMS as a root service_offer keyed by its exchange; it remains OBSERVED/observed/published and carries the retained source receipt, rather than becoming a presentation-owned row
  forbidden_inference an observed lot -> the thing exists, is in stock, is the seller's to sell, or is still obtainable
  forbidden_inference a listing this estate shows -> a price, an offer, or terms available to any particular buyer
  forbidden_inference showing an exchange -> this estate performing any part of it
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCommerce/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/service_offer.json
  source_path scripts/project_listings.py.archive
  source_path scripts/project_listings.mjs
  source_path scripts/publish_market.py.archive
  source_path scripts/publish_market.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/project_listings_owner.test.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/publish_market_owner.test.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/project_listings_owner_test.py.archive
  source_path scripts/tests/publish_market_owner_test.py.archive
  witness scripts/tests/project_listings_owner.test.mjs proves repeated listing projection writes one CMS-owned observed offer without duplicating it
  witness scripts/tests/publish_market_owner.test.mjs proves the market page reads the canonical CMS offer and excludes a disagreeing legacy commerce_lot
  witness 2026-09-19 bringatrailer.com had been admitted and filed under news; 48 lots were typed as commerce and 1 editorial post in the same feed was left alone, establishing 96 stages through the organ with none refused
  witness 2026-09-19 the organ refuses a skipped stage in practice: recording payment on a fresh exchange answers "payment requires commitment to be established first", and product then listing succeeds, leaving 13 outstanding each naming its owner
  witness 2026-09-19 /market publishes the chain for every observed lot at aurekai.shop and the other worker-served territories, showing established stages with what each still does not establish
  witness 2026-09-22 the local estate projected 48 dated Bring a Trailer observations to 48 unique root service_offer rows, all OBSERVED/observed/published, established 96 lawful commerce stages with none refused, and rendered a 48-lot market page from those owner rows; project_listings_owner_test proves a repeat pass updates rather than duplicates and publish_market_owner_test proves a disagreeing commerce_lot compatibility row cannot reach the public page
  witness 2026-09-29 scripts/tests/publish_market_owner_test.py.archive with BONFYRE_VERIFY_LEGACY=1 proved the Bun renderer emitted the same owner-backed market HTML byte-for-byte as the historical Python renderer while refusing the stale commerce_lot row
  known_gap bf_commerce_record had no caller anywhere in the estate before this; the chain was measured against all 225 stage pairs and run by nothing, so this is its first use rather than a long-standing path
  known_gap no price is observed for any lot: the feeds carry titles and addresses only, and reading a lot page for its current bid is a further observation this estate has not made
  known_gap only five marketplaces have a lot-address pattern, so a shopping feed outside that list is still read as whatever it was filed as
  interacts marketplace-observation-prices-through-the-membrane

interaction marketplace-observation-prices-through-the-membrane
  source marketplace-observation
  destination financial-metabolism
  relation observed_price_is_not_an_accrual
  preserves the separation between what this estate's own reading costs and what a merchant asks for a thing it is selling
  drops any path by which a merchant's asking price could enter this estate's accrued use, or an accrual could be read as an amount owed to a merchant
  forbidden_inference a price observed in a listing -> a cost this estate incurred, an amount it owes, or a price it offers
  witness 2026-09-19 /market and /economics are separate surfaces that link to each other; no lot price enters the meter, and no metered accrual appears against a lot
